Z||000009||avengador1||11-19-2001||09:37 AM||||The greatest cost in making a model is the price of the molds and their frames. This cost is usually in the thousands of dollars(could even be in the tens of thousands depending on how many molds are made and their size). If the initial investment has already been made, which it has because the molds exist, then the only costs left are the plastics used to mold, machine time and secondary operations, such as plating of the chrome pieces and packageing. It should be easy to remake the models in plastic again, and relatively cheap, that is if the molds still exist.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
